A||||7||fierogt88||torque convertor lockup||||1||
Z||000000||fierogt88||12-20-2000||03:33 PM||||By doing my research into the fiero I was able to get a good deal (I think) on my 88 gt.  It was having transmission problems, which I was able to identify as the common torque convertor solenoid problem.  I bought the car and took it to my mechanic, who agreed with the prognosis and fixed it.  The problem seemed to go away.  Now that it has gotten colder, however, I need to "warm-up" the transmission, or else it will stall when going into R or D.  Once it is warmed up I don't have any other symptoms.  Can anybody tell me if I have another solenoid going bad or could this be related to something else?||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||12-20-2000||06:36 PM||||The stalling is probably related to something else. The TCC cannot come on until the car is in third gear.  The stalling is probably due to a coolant temperature sensor $10, vacuum leak, sticky/leaking EGR valve, or it just needs a tune-up. I would try the coolant temp first.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||12-20-2000||08:48 PM||||IF you don't know when the transmission fluid was last changed you might want to do that now.  The old fluid could be very dirty.  I thought I remeber that a delay between N and D can be caused by a clogged transmisison filter.<P>When I bought my daughter's 87 Coupe it had 156K on it.  I had my local shop first change the transmission filter.  After refilling the fluid to the proper level, I then had them do a complete flush of the system with their filter exchange machine to get rid of virtually all the old transmission fluid.  Remember that during a filter repalcement about 1/2 of the old fluid is still in the transmission.  Her car is still shifting great so far.<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierogt88||12-21-2000||11:07 AM||||I had the fluid and filter changed when the solenoid was changed, less than 2 months ago.  I doubt this is the source of my problem.  Actually, there is one other symptom that I forgot to mention... the car pulls at idle.  Without giving any gas it will cruise at about 15mph.  If anyone has any more info, I would appreciate it.  In the meantime I will check out the coolant temp sensor and EGR.  Since everything else works fine (except my stuck temp guage) I doubt if its a tune-up issue or vacuum leak.  This gives me some things to look at though. Thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||bubbajoexx||12-21-2000||10:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierogt88:<BR><B>I had the fluid and filter changed when the solenoid was changed, less than 2 months ago.  I doubt this is the source of my problem.  Actually, there is one other symptom that I forgot to mention... the car pulls at idle.  Without giving any gas it will cruise at about 15mph.  If anyone has any more info, I would appreciate it.  In the meantime I will check out the coolant temp sensor and EGR.  Since everything else works fine (except my stuck temp guage) I doubt if its a tune-up issue or vacuum leak.  This gives me some things to look at though. Thanks   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>change the torque converter the clutch trust bearings are starting to fail  I just had one fail on me I have the lockup converter disabled in mine  the bearings failed  and the engine would not disengage from the trans when the car was running. changed the converter now its all fine.||||reg||1
Z||000005||BAM-BAM||12-22-2000||12:21 AM||||  Well now, hold on there. Don't go gett'n yerself all distorted over nothin, or very little at most. With the drop in tempreture it would be normal to have a warm up period. Remember these cars ar at least 13 years old. From what I can remember, WV is rather cool this time of year. As for the pullin at idle, what are your neutral idle RPM's. It may be as simple as, you need to let it warm up first. In colder temps the idle will stay high for a period of time untill the coolant temp sensor says otherwise. Your car may be suffering from Hellacoldous Climatous. Let it warm up for about 5-10 minutes and see if problems persist. Let's not run you into the poor house just yet. Let us know how it turns out!!!<P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||12
Z||000006||fierogt88||12-22-2000||09:02 AM||||It took about 10 minutes in 40 degree weather to warm up enough.  I'm not surprised that it has a warm up period at its age, but this seems a little excessive to me.  On startup my idle is about 2000 ~ 2100.  After warming up it drops around 1400 ~ 1500.  The pull at idle seems to be constant, but I haven't driven this car for more than 10 minutes at a time yet.  I am actually worried that the torque converter is going south, because when it stalls it stalls hard, just like it did with the bad solenoid.  I will work on the temp sensor/EGR this weekend and keep you guys posted.  And thanks.  This forum is the best.  If I hadn't found you guys when researching my "fun" vehicle I probably would have ended up with a camaro or (heaven's, do I say it?) a mudstain!<P>Oh, one last thing, my stuck temp guage wouldn't be attached to that temp sensor would it?  Since there are like 3 temp sensors in there somewhere, we gotta be talking about different sensors... ||||reg||1
Z||000007||ThatRickGuy||12-22-2000||10:33 AM||||Your temp guage runs off a different sensor  (the one back by the coil) But your idle seems a little high, you may want to get some carb cleaner and check for vac leaks and check out the EGR tube, if it's cracked it can make the engine idle high. That high idle could be causing the pull too. As for the hard stall, well, I'd say check the previous mentioned things, then go for the tranny fluid change, and if it's still doing it, the look into the convert (read: cheepest/easiest first!)||||reg||1
